---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const pageTitle = "Siding & Exterior Finishes | Appalachian Sheds Inc.";
const pageDescription = "Compare five Appalachian Sheds siding systems, wall assemblies, exterior details and architectural finishes.";
---
<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
<Fragment set:html={"<section class=\"asi-page-hero\"><div class=\"asi-shell\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Options &amp; Upgrades \u00b7 Exterior Materials</div><h1>Siding &amp; Exterior Finishes</h1><p>Five carefully selected siding systems, each with its own appearance, construction method, and architectural character.</p></div></section><div class=\"asi-shell\"><p class=\"asi-review-note\">Review edition: five approved siding categories and original technical descriptions have been retained. Five photo positions await the actual product images. Current construction specification conflicts must be resolved before production publication.</p></div><section aria-labelledby=\"asi-siding-master-title\" id=\"asi-siding-master\">\n<div class=\"sm-shell\">\n<!-- ========================================================\n         CATEGORY INTRODUCTION\n         ======================================================== -->\n<header class=\"sm-head\">\n<p class=\"sm-kicker\">Appalachian Sheds Inc. \u00b7 Siding &amp; Exterior Finishes</p>\n<h2 class=\"sm-title\" id=\"asi-siding-master-title\">Five Distinctive Ways to Finish Your Building</h2>\n<p class=\"sm-subtitle\">Choose the Exterior Character That Fits Your Building</p>\n<p class=\"sm-lede\">The siding you choose does more than establish color. It determines the texture, shadow lines, architectural character, maintenance profile and construction of the finished exterior. Appalachian Sheds offers five carefully selected siding systems\u2014each different enough to give you a meaningful choice without turning the process into an overwhelming catalog.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sm-divider\"></div>\n</header>\n<div class=\"sm-intro\">\n<div class=\"sm-intro-copy\">\n<h3>Start With the Look You Want</h3>\n<p>Some homeowners want the straightforward vertical character of a traditional wood shed. Others want deeper board-and-batten shadow lines, a residential horizontal lap profile, or the low-maintenance familiarity of vinyl siding.</p>\n<p>There is no single siding that is best for every building. The better choice is the siding system that fits the architecture, use, maintenance expectations and appearance you want for your property.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-intro-side\">\n<h3>Then Look Behind the Finish</h3>\n<p>Two buildings can appear equally attractive from the outside and still have very different wall assemblies underneath. That is why every Appalachian siding description also explains how the material is installed, what supports it and what preparation belongs behind the visible finish.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         FIVE SIDING SELECTOR\n         ======================================================== -->\n<div class=\"sm-selector-head\">\n<span>Our Five Siding Systems</span>\n<h3>Compare the Architectural Character First</h3>\n<p>Use these five choices as a starting point. Each detailed section explains the appearance, construction, backing, installation method and best applications for that siding.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-grid\">\n<!-- OPTION 01 -->\n<article class=\"sm-card\">\n<span class=\"sm-card-num\">01</span>\n<h4>LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding</h4>\n<span class=\"sm-card-type\">Structural Engineered-Wood Panel</span>\n<p>Clean vertical lines and traditional shed or barn character without applied battens. A straightforward engineered-wood exterior that allows doors, windows and rooflines to remain the primary architectural features.</p>\n<div class=\"sm-card-meta\">\n<b>Wall System</b>\n<span>Qualifying structural siding panel can form the continuous exterior wall skin.</span>\n</div>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-lpvp\">Explore Vertical Panel</a>\n</article>\n<!-- OPTION 02 -->\n<article class=\"sm-card\">\n<span class=\"sm-card-num\">02</span>\n<h4>Roseburg DuraTemp Wood Siding</h4>\n<span class=\"sm-card-type\">Real-Wood Plywood Structural Siding</span>\n<p>A plywood-based siding panel with a durable hardboard face and traditional rough-sawn character. Particularly well suited to classic sheds, barns, workshops and other buildings where authentic wood character matters.</p>\n<div class=\"sm-card-meta\">\n<b>Wall System</b>\n<span>The DuraTemp plywood siding panel itself can provide the structural exterior wall skin.</span>\n</div>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-dt\">Explore DuraTemp</a>\n</article>\n<!-- OPTION 03 -->\n<article class=\"sm-card\">\n<span class=\"sm-card-num\">03</span>\n<h4>LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten Siding</h4>\n<span class=\"sm-card-type\">Architectural Vertical Siding System</span>\n<p>Vertical siding with raised battens creates deeper shadow lines and greater architectural dimension for cottages, studios, pool houses, barns and premium custom buildings.</p>\n<div class=\"sm-card-meta\">\n<b>Wall System</b>\n<span>Applied over Appalachian Sheds' full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood-sheathed wall.</span>\n</div>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-bb\">Explore Board &amp; Batten</a>\n</article>\n<!-- OPTION 04 -->\n<article class=\"sm-card\">\n<span class=\"sm-card-num\">04</span>\n<h4>Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap Siding</h4>\n<span class=\"sm-card-type\">Low-Maintenance Horizontal Cladding</span>\n<p>Traditional residential horizontal lap styling with the low routine maintenance associated with vinyl. A natural choice when the backyard building should coordinate with a conventionally sided home.</p>\n<div class=\"sm-card-meta\">\n<b>Wall System</b>\n<span>Vinyl cladding installed over full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood, WRB and flashing.</span>\n</div>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-vinyl\">Explore Forest Ridge Vinyl</a>\n</article>\n<!-- OPTION 05 -->\n<article class=\"sm-card\">\n<span class=\"sm-card-num\">05</span>\n<h4>LP SmartSide Lap Siding</h4>\n<span class=\"sm-card-type\">Premium Horizontal Engineered Wood</span>\n<p>Horizontal engineered-wood siding for a refined residential or cottage-inspired exterior. Particularly effective on studios, offices, pool houses and other buildings designed to visually complement the home.</p>\n<div class=\"sm-card-meta\">\n<b>Wall System</b>\n<span>Installed by Appalachian Sheds over full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood and weather preparation.</span>\n</div>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-lap\">Explore LP Lap Siding</a>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         WHAT IS BEHIND THE SIDING?\n         ======================================================== -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"sm-wall-title\" class=\"sm-wall\">\n<div class=\"sm-wall-inner\">\n<div class=\"sm-wall-head\">\n<span>Construction Matters</span>\n<h3 id=\"sm-wall-title\">What's Behind the Siding?</h3>\n<p>The answer depends upon the siding. Some exterior products are structural siding panels themselves. Others are finish materials that depend upon a separately sheathed and weather-prepared wall underneath.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-wall-grid\">\n<div class=\"sm-wall-card\">\n<strong>Structural Siding Panels</strong>\n<p>LP SmartSide Vertical Panel and Roseburg DuraTemp can serve as the continuous structural exterior wall panel in qualifying installations. The siding panel itself therefore performs both an exterior-finish and structural wall-skin function.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-wall-card\">\n<strong>Applied Siding &amp; Cladding</strong>\n<p>LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten, Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge Vinyl and Appalachian's LP SmartSide Lap system are installed over a separately prepared continuous wall surface.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"sm-plywood\"><b>Appalachian Sheds Standard:</b> When a siding system uses separate structural wall sheathing, Appalachian Sheds uses full <b>1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood</b>. We make that specification visible because the wall behind the siding is an important part of the building\u2014even though it disappears from view when construction is complete.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         LP SMARTSIDE TRIM & FASCIA\n         ======================================================== -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"sm-trim-title\" class=\"sm-trim\">\n<div class=\"sm-trim-top\">\n<div class=\"sm-trim-copy\">\n<span class=\"sm-trim-kicker\">Exterior Trim &amp; Architectural Finish</span>\n<h3 id=\"sm-trim-title\">LP SmartSide Trim &amp; Fascia</h3>\n<p>The siding establishes the broad exterior surface, but the trim defines the architecture. Corner boards, door trim, window trim, fascia and other exterior details create the lines that frame the building and give it a finished appearance.</p>\n<p>Appalachian Sheds uses LP SmartSide engineered-wood trim products where our design calls for painted exterior trim. LP offers the visual character of traditional wood trim with the consistency of an engineered product specifically manufactured for exterior exposure.</p>\n<p>The system is available in Cedar Texture and Brushed Smooth profiles, multiple widths and thicknesses, and long 16-foot lengths that can reduce joints and visible seams on many building applications.</p>\n</div>\n<aside class=\"sm-trim-side\">\n<span>Why We Specify It</span>\n<strong>Wood Character Without Depending on Untreated Natural Trim</strong>\n<p>LP SmartSide Trim &amp; Fascia is treated through LP's SmartGuard process for resistance to termites and fungal decay and added protection against moisture, hail and freeze/thaw exposure. It also coordinates directly with LP SmartSide siding textures and factory-finish colors.</p>\n</aside>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-trim-benefits\">\n<div class=\"sm-trim-benefit\">\n<strong>Engineered Consistency</strong>\n<span>Manufactured widths, thicknesses and textures provide a predictable exterior-trim profile from piece to piece.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-trim-benefit\">\n<strong>SmartGuard Protection</strong>\n<span>Engineered for resistance to termites and fungal decay and protection from common exterior weather exposure.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-trim-benefit\">\n<strong>16-Foot Lengths</strong>\n<span>Long trim boards can reduce joints and seams and help create cleaner continuous architectural lines.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-trim-benefit\">\n<strong>Coordinated Appearance</strong>\n<span>Cedar Texture, Brushed Smooth and multiple finish choices make it easy to coordinate or contrast with the siding.</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-cedar\">\n<strong>How Does LP SmartSide Trim Compare With Natural Cedar?</strong>\n<p>Western Red Cedar remains a respected premium exterior wood and can provide excellent service when properly selected, detailed, finished and maintained. The difference is predictability and upkeep. Natural cedar changes appearance as it weathers, and exterior stains or coatings require periodic inspection and renewal. LP SmartSide Trim provides a manufactured, treated and paint-ready alternative with consistent dimensions, coordinated textures and long available lengths. For Appalachian Sheds' painted trim applications, those characteristics make LP SmartSide Trim &amp; Fascia an excellent fit.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         QUICK DECISION GUIDE\n         ======================================================== -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"sm-guide-title\" class=\"sm-guide\">\n<div class=\"sm-guide-head\">\n<span>Quick Decision Guide</span>\n<h3 id=\"sm-guide-title\">Start With the Exterior Character You Prefer</h3>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-guide-grid\">\n<div class=\"sm-guide-card\">\n<b>Clean &amp; Traditional</b>\n<span>LP SmartSide Vertical Panel</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-guide-card\">\n<b>Real-Wood Character</b>\n<span>Roseburg DuraTemp</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-guide-card\">\n<b>Architectural &amp; Dimensional</b>\n<span>LP Board &amp; Batten</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-guide-card\">\n<b>Residential &amp; Low Maintenance</b>\n<span>Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-guide-card\">\n<b>Residential Engineered Wood</b>\n<span>LP SmartSide Lap</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         FOOTER\n         ======================================================== -->\n<section class=\"sm-footer\">\n<div class=\"sm-footer-copy\">\n<span>Siding &amp; Exterior Finishes</span>\n<h3>Choose the Finish. Understand the Construction Behind It.</h3>\n<p>Our goal is not simply to show five attractive siding samples. We want you to understand what each material is, how it changes the appearance of the building, how it is installed and what supports it. That makes the exterior decision easier to understand\u2014and makes it easier to compare buildings on more than appearance alone.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sm-footer-side\">\n<strong>5 Siding Systems<br/>LP SmartSide Trim &amp; Fascia<br/>One Complete Exterior</strong>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-siding-lpvp-title\" id=\"asi-siding-lpvp\">\n<div class=\"lpvp-shell\">\n<header class=\"lpvp-head\">\n<p class=\"lpvp-kicker\">Siding &amp; Exterior Finishes \u00b7 Option 01</p>\n<h2 class=\"lpvp-title\" id=\"asi-siding-lpvp-title\">LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding</h2>\n<p class=\"lpvp-subtitle\">Clean Vertical Lines \u00b7 Engineered-Wood Construction</p>\n<p class=\"lpvp-lede\">LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding gives an Appalachian building the straightforward character of traditional vertical wood siding with the consistency of an engineered exterior panel. This option refers to qualifying large-format LP SmartSide structural Panel Siding\u2014not the separate nonstructural LP SmartSide Vertical Siding used in our Board &amp; Batten assembly. Its clean lines work especially well on classic sheds, garden buildings, workshops, barns and other structures where the architecture should remain simple, substantial and timeless.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"lpvp-divider\"></div>\n</header><figure aria-label=\"Image position for LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding\" class=\"asi-siding-photo-slot\" id=\"siding-photo-01\"><div class=\"asi-siding-photo-placeholder\"><span class=\"asi-slot-small\">PHOTOGRAPH POSITION 01 / 05</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-slot-icon\">\u25a7</span><strong>LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding</strong><span class=\"asi-slot-note\">Approved installed-finish photograph to be supplied</span></div><figcaption><strong>LP Vertical Panel \u2014 Installed Finish</strong><span>Illustration position reserved; no substitute product photograph used.</span></figcaption></figure>\n<div class=\"lpvp-intro-grid\">\n<article class=\"lpvp-copy\">\n<h3 class=\"lpvp-h3\">A Traditional Exterior Without Excess Decoration</h3>\n<p>Vertical panel siding creates strong proportions without competing with the building itself. Rooflines, doors, windows, trim, porches and overhangs remain the primary architectural features while the siding provides a consistent wood-grain background.</p>\n<p>For homeowners who want an Appalachian shed or small building to look purposeful rather than ornamental, this is one of the most versatile exterior treatments we offer.</p>\n</article>\n<aside aria-label=\"Architectural character\" class=\"lpvp-character\">\n<span class=\"lpvp-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Traditional. Clean. Understated. Versatile.</h3>\n<p>A strong choice for buildings where classic shed, barn or workshop character is more important than a highly decorative exterior.</p>\n<div aria-label=\"Suitable building types\" class=\"lpvp-tags\">\n<span class=\"lpvp-tag\">Classic Sheds</span>\n<span class=\"lpvp-tag\">Garden Buildings</span>\n<span class=\"lpvp-tag\">Workshops</span>\n<span class=\"lpvp-tag\">Barn Styles</span>\n</div>\n</aside>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-benefits\">\n<div class=\"lpvp-benefit\">\n<strong>Vertical Profile</strong>\n<span>Creates the familiar proportions associated with traditional sheds, barns and utility buildings.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-benefit\">\n<strong>Engineered Wood</strong>\n<span>Manufactured as an engineered exterior siding panel rather than a thin decorative surface treatment.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-benefit\">\n<strong>Color Flexibility</strong>\n<span>Works naturally with warm neutrals, greens, earth tones and contrasting trim combinations.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-benefit\">\n<strong>Clean Detailing</strong>\n<span>Allows windows, doors, fascia, corner boards and other architectural details to stand out clearly.</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"lpvp-install-title\" class=\"lpvp-install\">\n<div class=\"lpvp-install-inner\">\n<div class=\"lpvp-install-copy\">\n<span class=\"lpvp-mini\">How We Install It</span>\n<h3 id=\"lpvp-install-title\">The Wall Behind the Finish Matters</h3>\n<p>LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding is different from an applied lap siding, vinyl cladding or the nonstructural LP SmartSide Vertical Siding used in our Board &amp; Batten system. Qualifying large-format LP SmartSide Panel Siding is designed so the panel itself can form the structural exterior skin of the framed wall when installed according to the manufacturer's requirements.</p>\n<p>The panels are installed vertically over properly spaced framing with the required panel spacing, fastening, exterior clearances, edge treatment and flashing details. Because the panel itself can provide the continuous structural wall surface, a second layer of plywood is not automatically required simply to support this siding.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-wall-card\">\n<p class=\"lpvp-wall-title\">Typical Appalachian Wall Assembly</p>\n<div class=\"lpvp-spec\">\n<b>Siding Type</b>\n<span>Qualifying large-format structural engineered-wood vertical panel siding</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-spec\">\n<b>Primary Backing</b>\n<span>Properly framed wall; qualifying panels may be installed directly to structural framing</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-spec\">\n<b>Preparation</b>\n<span>Correct panel spacing, fastening, flashing, sealed exposed edges and required exterior clearances</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-spec\">\n<b>Orientation</b>\n<span>Vertical panel installation</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-spec\">\n<b>Moisture Details</b>\n<span>Weather-resistive and flashing details appropriate to the specific building assembly and application</span>\n</div>\n<p class=\"lpvp-plywood-note\"><strong>Appalachian Sheds Standard:</strong> When a siding assembly requires or specifies separate wall sheathing, we use full <strong>1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood</strong> as our wall sheathing standard rather than relying on intermittent furring or minimum-thickness sheet products.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<div class=\"lpvp-best-grid\">\n<section class=\"lpvp-panel\">\n<h3>Well Suited For</h3>\n<ul class=\"lpvp-list\">\n<li>Traditional storage sheds</li>\n<li>Garden sheds and garden buildings</li>\n<li>Workshops and equipment buildings</li>\n<li>Barn-inspired structures</li>\n<li>Buildings where clean vertical proportions are preferred</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"lpvp-panel\">\n<h3>Why Homeowners Choose It</h3>\n<ul class=\"lpvp-list\">\n<li>Traditional wood-building appearance</li>\n<li>Simple vertical lines without applied battens</li>\n<li>Engineered-wood exterior construction</li>\n<li>Broad flexibility in siding and trim colors</li>\n<li>Works with both understated and contrasting trim schemes</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section class=\"lpvp-compare\">\n<h3>Vertical Panel or Board &amp; Batten?</h3>\n<p>These are intentionally offered as two different exterior treatments. LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding creates the cleaner and simpler appearance. LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten adds raised vertical battens that produce deeper shadow lines and greater architectural dimension. Customers wanting a straightforward traditional exterior will often prefer Vertical Panel Siding; customers wanting a more pronounced architectural treatment may prefer Board &amp; Batten.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"lpvp-footer\">\n<div class=\"lpvp-footer-copy\">\n<span>Choosing Your Exterior</span>\n<h3>A Premium Exterior Begins Before the Siding Is Visible</h3>\n<p>The finished siding is only one part of the exterior wall. Appalachian Sheds considers the framing, backing, moisture preparation, flashing, trim and final siding system as one complete assembly so the material you see is properly supported by the construction behind it.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lpvp-footer-side\">\n<strong>LP SmartSide<br/>Vertical Panel Siding<br/>Option 01 of 05</strong>\n</div>\n</section>\n<details class=\"lpvp-tech\">\n<summary>Technical Installation Note <b aria-hidden=\"true\"></b></summary>\n<div class=\"lpvp-tech-body\">\n<p>This option is based on qualifying LP SmartSide structural Panel Siding and should not be confused with the separate nonstructural LP SmartSide Vertical Siding used in Appalachian Sheds' Board &amp; Batten assembly. Panel Siding installation requirements vary by panel series, framing spacing, structural application and project conditions. Qualifying panel siding may be attached directly to structural framing or to approved wood structural panel sheathing when permitted by the applicable product instructions. Final fastening, flashing, spacing, clearance and moisture-management details are determined by the specific product and building assembly used on the project.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-siding-dt-title\" id=\"asi-siding-dt\">\n<div class=\"dt-shell\">\n<header class=\"dt-head\">\n<p class=\"dt-kicker\">Siding &amp; Exterior Finishes \u00b7 Option 02</p>\n<h2 class=\"dt-title\" id=\"asi-siding-dt-title\">Roseburg DuraTemp Wood Siding</h2>\n<p class=\"dt-subtitle\">Real Wood Construction \u00b7 Rough-Sawn Cedar Character</p>\n<p class=\"dt-lede\">Roseburg DuraTemp combines the strength of a plywood siding panel with a durable hardboard face and the textured appearance of rough-sawn cedar. It is especially well suited to traditional sheds, barns, workshops and other backyard buildings where genuine wood character and structural simplicity are both important.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"dt-divider\"></div>\n</header><figure aria-label=\"Image position for Roseburg DuraTemp Wood Siding\" class=\"asi-siding-photo-slot\" id=\"siding-photo-02\"><div class=\"asi-siding-photo-placeholder\"><span class=\"asi-slot-small\">PHOTOGRAPH POSITION 02 / 05</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-slot-icon\">\u25a7</span><strong>Roseburg DuraTemp Wood Siding</strong><span class=\"asi-slot-note\">Approved installed-finish photograph to be supplied</span></div><figcaption><strong>Roseburg DuraTemp \u2014 Installed Finish</strong><span>Illustration position reserved; no substitute product photograph used.</span></figcaption></figure>\n<div class=\"dt-intro-grid\">\n<article class=\"dt-copy\">\n<h3 class=\"dt-h3\">A Real-Wood Siding Panel Built for Outdoor Structures</h3>\n<p>DuraTemp is not a thin decorative cladding placed over another exterior wall surface. It is a plywood-based real-wood siding panel manufactured specifically for exterior applications.</p>\n<p>The hardboard face provides the rough-sawn visual character associated with traditional cedar siding while the plywood construction gives the panel the structural qualities needed for many shed and barn wall applications.</p>\n</article>\n<aside aria-label=\"Architectural character\" class=\"dt-character\">\n<span class=\"dt-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Authentic. Traditional. Textured. Purpose-Built.</h3>\n<p>DuraTemp works especially well when the building should retain the unmistakable character of a traditional wood shed, barn or workshop rather than a residential-cladding appearance.</p>\n<div aria-label=\"Suitable building types\" class=\"dt-tags\">\n<span class=\"dt-tag\">Classic Sheds</span>\n<span class=\"dt-tag\">Barns</span>\n<span class=\"dt-tag\">Workshops</span>\n<span class=\"dt-tag\">Garden Buildings</span>\n</div>\n</aside>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-benefits\">\n<div class=\"dt-benefit\">\n<strong>Real Wood</strong>\n<span>Plywood-based exterior siding rather than vinyl, fiber cement or an OSB-based decorative surface.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-benefit\">\n<strong>Rough-Sawn Look</strong>\n<span>A textured hardboard face provides the visual character of traditional rough-sawn cedar siding.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-benefit\">\n<strong>Structural Panel</strong>\n<span>Qualifying DuraTemp panels can form the continuous exterior structural skin of the framed wall.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-benefit\">\n<strong>Paintable Finish</strong>\n<span>Designed to accept an appropriate exterior coating system for long-term color and weather protection.</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"dt-install-title\" class=\"dt-install\">\n<div class=\"dt-install-inner\">\n<div class=\"dt-install-copy\">\n<span class=\"dt-mini\">How We Install It</span>\n<h3 id=\"dt-install-title\">The Siding Panel Is Also the Wall Skin</h3>\n<p>Roseburg DuraTemp is a structural plywood siding panel. When the selected panel span rating matches the wall framing layout, the siding can be installed vertically directly over the structural wall framing rather than requiring another layer of plywood solely to support the siding.</p>\n<p>The panels are installed with their edges supported by framing and with the manufacturer's required expansion spacing, corrosion-resistant fastening, exterior clearances and finish preparation. This creates a continuous real-wood exterior wall surface without adding an unnecessary second structural panel behind it.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-wall-card\">\n<p class=\"dt-wall-title\">Typical Appalachian Wall Assembly</p>\n<div class=\"dt-spec\">\n<b>Siding Type</b>\n<span>Real-wood plywood structural siding panel with hardboard face</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-spec\">\n<b>Primary Backing</b>\n<span>Properly framed structural wall; qualifying panels may install directly over the framing</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-spec\">\n<b>Panel Support</b>\n<span>Panel edges and ends are supported by framing, with framing spacing matched to the panel span rating</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-spec\">\n<b>Preparation</b>\n<span>Required panel spacing, corrosion-resistant fasteners, exterior clearances, sealed edges and proper finish preparation</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-spec\">\n<b>Orientation</b>\n<span>Vertical panel installation</span>\n</div>\n<p class=\"dt-plywood-note\"><strong>Important distinction:</strong> DuraTemp itself is already a plywood-based structural siding panel. For this wall system, adding another layer of plywood merely as siding backing would normally duplicate the structural panel that DuraTemp already provides.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<div class=\"dt-best-grid\">\n<section class=\"dt-panel\">\n<h3>Well Suited For</h3>\n<ul class=\"dt-list\">\n<li>Traditional storage sheds</li>\n<li>Garden sheds and garden buildings</li>\n<li>Workshops and equipment buildings</li>\n<li>Barn-inspired structures</li>\n<li>Buildings where authentic wood character is preferred</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"dt-panel\">\n<h3>Why Homeowners Choose It</h3>\n<ul class=\"dt-list\">\n<li>Real-wood plywood construction</li>\n<li>Traditional rough-sawn exterior texture</li>\n<li>Structural siding and exterior finish in one panel</li>\n<li>Suitable for painted exterior color schemes</li>\n<li>Long-established use on sheds, barns and residential structures</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section class=\"dt-compare\">\n<h3>DuraTemp or LP SmartSide Vertical Panel?</h3>\n<p>Both provide a clean vertical exterior and both can function as structural siding panels in qualifying installations, but the materials are different. DuraTemp is built around a real plywood panel with a hardboard face and a rough-sawn cedar appearance. LP SmartSide Vertical Panel is an engineered-wood siding product manufactured through LP's SmartGuard process. The choice is therefore less about which one is \u201cbetter\u201d and more about which material construction and exterior character best fit the building.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"dt-footer\">\n<div class=\"dt-footer-copy\">\n<span>Understanding the Wall Assembly</span>\n<h3>Not Every Premium Siding Needs a Separate Sheathing Layer</h3>\n<p>DuraTemp is a useful example of why exterior wall systems should be evaluated as complete assemblies. Because the siding itself is manufactured as a plywood structural panel, it can provide both the exterior siding surface and the continuous structural wall skin in an appropriate framed-wall installation.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"dt-footer-side\">\n<strong>Roseburg DuraTemp<br/>Wood Siding<br/>Option 02 of 05</strong>\n</div>\n</section>\n<details class=\"dt-tech\">\n<summary>Technical Installation Note <b aria-hidden=\"true\"></b></summary>\n<div class=\"dt-tech-body\">\n<p>Roseburg permits DuraTemp siding panels to be installed vertically directly over wall framing when the framing spacing does not exceed the span rating shown on the panel. Panel edges and ends are supported by framing, appropriate expansion spacing is maintained, corrosion-resistant fasteners are used, and the siding is finished and maintained according to the manufacturer's current instructions. Specific installation requirements remain subject to the particular panel selected and the final building assembly.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-siding-bb-title\" id=\"asi-siding-bb\">\n<div class=\"bb-shell\">\n<header class=\"bb-head\">\n<p class=\"bb-kicker\">Siding &amp; Exterior Finishes \u00b7 Option 03</p>\n<h2 class=\"bb-title\" id=\"asi-siding-bb-title\">LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten Siding</h2>\n<p class=\"bb-subtitle\">Dimensional Vertical Siding \u00b7 Full Plywood-Backed Wall Assembly</p>\n<p class=\"bb-lede\">LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten gives an Appalachian building a more architectural vertical exterior with deep shadow lines, raised battens and the character associated with traditional barns, cottages and modern farmhouse design. Unlike structural panel siding, our board-and-batten system is installed as an applied siding assembly over a fully sheathed exterior wall.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"bb-divider\"></div>\n</header><figure aria-label=\"Image position for LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten Siding\" class=\"asi-siding-photo-slot\" id=\"siding-photo-03\"><div class=\"asi-siding-photo-placeholder\"><span class=\"asi-slot-small\">PHOTOGRAPH POSITION 03 / 05</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-slot-icon\">\u25a7</span><strong>LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten Siding</strong><span class=\"asi-slot-note\">Approved installed-finish photograph to be supplied</span></div><figcaption><strong>LP Board &amp; Batten \u2014 Installed Finish</strong><span>Illustration position reserved; no substitute product photograph used.</span></figcaption></figure>\n<div class=\"bb-intro-grid\">\n<article class=\"bb-copy\">\n<h3 class=\"bb-h3\">More Depth Than a Flat Vertical Panel</h3>\n<p>Board-and-batten siding gets its distinctive appearance from the relationship between wider vertical siding boards and narrower raised battens. Those battens create deeper shadow lines and a stronger sense of craftsmanship than a simple flat panel exterior.</p>\n<p>It is especially effective on buildings with pronounced rooflines, porches, transom windows, premium doors, timber details and other architectural features where the siding should contribute to the overall design rather than simply cover the wall.</p>\n</article>\n<aside aria-label=\"Architectural character\" class=\"bb-character\">\n<span class=\"bb-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Dimensional. Crafted. Traditional. Architectural.</h3>\n<p>Board &amp; Batten works especially well when the building is intended to have more visual depth and architectural presence than a conventional storage structure.</p>\n<div aria-label=\"Suitable building types\" class=\"bb-tags\">\n<span class=\"bb-tag\">Country Cottages</span>\n<span class=\"bb-tag\">Custom Buildings</span>\n<span class=\"bb-tag\">Pool Houses</span>\n<span class=\"bb-tag\">Barn Styles</span>\n</div>\n</aside>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-benefits\">\n<div class=\"bb-benefit\">\n<strong>Deep Shadow Lines</strong>\n<span>Raised battens add visible depth and dimension that flat vertical panel siding does not provide.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-benefit\">\n<strong>Architectural Detail</strong>\n<span>Pairs naturally with premium doors, windows, porches, roof overhangs and timber accents.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-benefit\">\n<strong>Engineered Wood</strong>\n<span>Uses LP SmartSide engineered-wood siding and trim components for a coordinated exterior system.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-benefit\">\n<strong>Solid Wall Backing</strong>\n<span>Installed over a continuously sheathed wall rather than depending on intermittent horizontal furring.</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"bb-install-title\" class=\"bb-install\">\n<div class=\"bb-install-inner\">\n<div class=\"bb-install-copy\">\n<span class=\"bb-mini\">How We Install It</span>\n<h3 id=\"bb-install-title\">A Fully Sheathed Wall Comes First</h3>\n<p>LP SmartSide Vertical Siding is an applied siding product rather than a structural wall panel. LP requires this system to be installed over continuous wood structural panel sheathing with the appropriate weather-resistive barrier behind the siding.</p>\n<p>Appalachian Sheds prepares that wall with full <strong>1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing</strong>. The weather-resistive layer and flashing details are installed over the prepared wall, followed by the vertical LP SmartSide siding and properly laid-out LP battens that create the finished board-and-batten appearance.</p>\n<p>This means the exterior is supported by a continuous plywood-backed wall assembly rather than treating widely spaced furring strips as the primary siding support.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-wall-card\">\n<p class=\"bb-wall-title\">Typical Appalachian Wall Assembly</p>\n<div class=\"bb-spec\">\n<b>Siding Type</b>\n<span>Nonstructural LP SmartSide Vertical Siding with applied LP SmartSide battens</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-spec\">\n<b>Wall Backing</b>\n<span>Full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing over the structural wall framing</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-spec\">\n<b>Moisture Layer</b>\n<span>Properly installed weather-resistive barrier integrated with window, door and wall flashing</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-spec\">\n<b>Finish Layer</b>\n<span>Vertical LP SmartSide siding installed over the prepared wall</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-spec\">\n<b>Architectural Detail</b>\n<span>LP SmartSide battens installed vertically to create the finished board-and-batten profile</span>\n</div>\n<p class=\"bb-plywood-note\"><strong>Appalachian Sheds Standard:</strong> LP calls for a minimum 7/16-category wood structural panel behind its Vertical Siding. Appalachian Sheds instead uses full <strong>1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood</strong> as our continuous wall-sheathing specification for this siding system.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"bb-assembly-title\" class=\"bb-assembly\">\n<div class=\"bb-assembly-head\">\n<span>From the Framing Out</span>\n<h3 id=\"bb-assembly-title\">Understanding the Board &amp; Batten Wall</h3>\n<p>The finished battens are only the outermost architectural detail. The performance of the exterior begins with the complete wall assembly behind them.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-layers\">\n<div class=\"bb-layer\">\n<span class=\"bb-layer-num\">1</span>\n<strong>Wall Framing</strong>\n<span>The structural framework that establishes the wall.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-layer\">\n<span class=\"bb-layer-num\">2</span>\n<strong>1/2\" Plywood</strong>\n<span>Continuous exterior-grade plywood sheathing across the framed wall.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-layer\">\n<span class=\"bb-layer-num\">3</span>\n<strong>Weather Layer</strong>\n<span>WRB and flashing details integrated into the exterior wall assembly.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-layer\">\n<span class=\"bb-layer-num\">4</span>\n<strong>Vertical Siding</strong>\n<span>LP SmartSide Vertical Siding applied over the prepared wall.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-layer\">\n<span class=\"bb-layer-num\">5</span>\n<strong>Raised Battens</strong>\n<span>LP trim battens create the characteristic depth and vertical shadow lines.</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<div class=\"bb-best-grid\">\n<section class=\"bb-panel\">\n<h3>Well Suited For</h3>\n<ul class=\"bb-list\">\n<li>Country cottage and farmhouse-inspired buildings</li>\n<li>Premium garden buildings</li>\n<li>Pool houses and backyard retreats</li>\n<li>Studios and backyard offices</li>\n<li>Barns and larger custom buildings</li>\n<li>Projects where architectural appearance is a priority</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"bb-panel\">\n<h3>Why Homeowners Choose It</h3>\n<ul class=\"bb-list\">\n<li>Greater architectural depth than flat panel siding</li>\n<li>Distinctive vertical shadow lines</li>\n<li>Traditional barn and cottage character</li>\n<li>Engineered-wood siding and trim components</li>\n<li>Full plywood-backed Appalachian wall assembly</li>\n<li>Strong compatibility with contrasting trim colors</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section class=\"bb-compare\">\n<h3>Board &amp; Batten or Vertical Panel?</h3>\n<p>Although both create strong vertical lines, the two Appalachian siding systems are constructed differently. LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding uses a structural panel that can form the exterior wall skin itself in qualifying applications. Our LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten system uses separate Vertical Siding and raised battens installed over a fully prepared 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood-sheathed wall. The result is greater visual depth, stronger shadow lines and a more architectural exterior.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"bb-footer\">\n<div class=\"bb-footer-copy\">\n<span>What's Behind the Siding Matters</span>\n<h3>The Finished Exterior Starts With a Solid Wall</h3>\n<p>Board &amp; Batten is visually distinctive, but the important construction difference is behind the visible siding. Appalachian Sheds builds this system over a continuous 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood wall, then adds the proper weather preparation, vertical siding and battens to complete the exterior.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bb-footer-side\">\n<strong>LP SmartSide<br/>Board &amp; Batten Siding<br/>Option 03 of 05</strong>\n</div>\n</section>\n<details class=\"bb-tech\">\n<summary>Technical Installation Note <b aria-hidden=\"true\"></b></summary>\n<div class=\"bb-tech-body\">\n<p>LP SmartSide Vertical Siding is not rated as structural siding and is intended for installation over continuous wood structural panel sheathing. LP currently specifies a minimum 7/16-category wood structural panel and a properly installed weather-resistive barrier behind the siding. Appalachian Sheds' specification for this wall system is full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing, followed by the appropriate moisture-management and flashing details, LP SmartSide Vertical Siding, and LP SmartSide trim battens installed according to the applicable product instructions.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-siding-vinyl-title\" id=\"asi-siding-vinyl\">\n<div class=\"vinyl-shell\">\n<header class=\"vinyl-head\">\n<p class=\"vinyl-kicker\">Siding &amp; Exterior Finishes \u00b7 Option 04</p>\n<h2 class=\"vinyl-title\" id=\"asi-siding-vinyl-title\">Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap Siding</h2>\n<p class=\"vinyl-subtitle\">Traditional Horizontal Lap \u00b7 Low-Maintenance Exterior</p>\n<p class=\"vinyl-lede\">Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge gives an Appalachian building the familiar horizontal lines of traditional residential lap siding with the low-maintenance advantages of vinyl. The finished appearance is clean and residential, but the quality of the wall beneath the vinyl is just as important as the siding itself.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"vinyl-divider\"></div>\n</header><figure aria-label=\"Image position for Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap Siding\" class=\"asi-siding-photo-slot\" id=\"siding-photo-04\"><div class=\"asi-siding-photo-placeholder\"><span class=\"asi-slot-small\">PHOTOGRAPH POSITION 04 / 05</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-slot-icon\">\u25a7</span><strong>Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap Siding</strong><span class=\"asi-slot-note\">Approved installed-finish photograph to be supplied</span></div><figcaption><strong>Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap \u2014 Installed Finish</strong><span>Illustration position reserved; no substitute product photograph used.</span></figcaption></figure>\n<div class=\"vinyl-intro-grid\">\n<article class=\"vinyl-copy\">\n<h3 class=\"vinyl-h3\">A More Residential Exterior Character</h3>\n<p>Forest Ridge differs visually from our vertical wood and engineered-wood siding options. Its horizontal lap profile creates the familiar appearance commonly seen on homes, cottages and residential accessory buildings.</p>\n<p>That makes it particularly attractive when the goal is to coordinate the backyard building with the architecture of the home or create a cleaner, lower-maintenance residential appearance.</p>\n</article>\n<aside aria-label=\"Architectural character\" class=\"vinyl-character\">\n<span class=\"vinyl-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Residential. Familiar. Clean. Low Maintenance.</h3>\n<p>Forest Ridge is a strong choice when the building should visually relate to a traditionally sided home rather than emphasize barn or utility-building character.</p>\n<div aria-label=\"Suitable building types\" class=\"vinyl-tags\">\n<span class=\"vinyl-tag\">Cottages</span>\n<span class=\"vinyl-tag\">Pool Houses</span>\n<span class=\"vinyl-tag\">Garden Buildings</span>\n<span class=\"vinyl-tag\">Storage Sheds</span>\n</div>\n</aside>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-benefits\">\n<div class=\"vinyl-benefit\">\n<strong>Traditional Lap</strong>\n<span>Horizontal siding courses create the familiar proportions of conventional residential siding.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-benefit\">\n<strong>Low Maintenance</strong>\n<span>Does not require routine scraping, painting or staining to maintain the exterior finish.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-benefit\">\n<strong>Wood-Grain Finish</strong>\n<span>A textured surface gives the siding more visual character than a completely smooth vinyl panel.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-benefit\">\n<strong>Continuous Backing</strong>\n<span>Installed over a fully sheathed, weather-prepared wall rather than treated as a structural wall material.</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"vinyl-install-title\" class=\"vinyl-install\">\n<div class=\"vinyl-install-inner\">\n<div class=\"vinyl-install-copy\">\n<span class=\"vinyl-mini\">How We Install It</span>\n<h3 id=\"vinyl-install-title\">Vinyl Is the Finish \u2014 Not the Wall</h3>\n<p>Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap Siding is an exterior cladding. It does not replace structural wall sheathing and should be installed over a smooth, flat and stable wall surface.</p>\n<p>Appalachian Sheds first sheathes the framed wall with full <strong>1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood</strong>. The wall is then prepared with the appropriate weather-resistive barrier and flashing before starter strips, corner components, trim channels and the horizontal vinyl siding courses are installed.</p>\n<p>The result is a finished vinyl exterior supported by a continuous plywood-backed wall rather than asking the vinyl itself\u2014or intermittent framing\u2014to perform a job it was never designed to do.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-wall-card\">\n<p class=\"vinyl-wall-title\">Typical Appalachian Wall Assembly</p>\n<div class=\"vinyl-spec\">\n<b>Siding Type</b>\n<span>Nonstructural Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge vinyl exterior cladding</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-spec\">\n<b>Wall Backing</b>\n<span>Full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing over the structural wall framing</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-spec\">\n<b>Moisture Layer</b>\n<span>Continuous weather-resistive barrier with properly integrated flashing at openings and transitions</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-spec\">\n<b>Accessories</b>\n<span>Starter strips, corners, J-channels and other required vinyl trim components</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-spec\">\n<b>Finish Layer</b>\n<span>Horizontal Forest Ridge Traditional Lap siding installed with proper fastening and movement allowance</span>\n</div>\n<p class=\"vinyl-plywood-note\"><strong>Appalachian Sheds Standard:</strong> Vinyl siding can be installed over several approved sheathing materials. Appalachian Sheds uses full <strong>1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood</strong> as our continuous wall backing rather than reducing the wall assembly to minimum-thickness OSB.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"vinyl-assembly-title\" class=\"vinyl-assembly\">\n<div class=\"vinyl-assembly-head\">\n<span>From the Framing Out</span>\n<h3 id=\"vinyl-assembly-title\">Understanding the Vinyl-Sided Wall</h3>\n<p>The vinyl is the visible finish. The strength, flatness and moisture preparation of the wall beneath it are established before the first siding course is installed.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-layers\">\n<div class=\"vinyl-layer\">\n<span class=\"vinyl-layer-num\">1</span>\n<strong>Wall Framing</strong>\n<span>The structural wall framework is built straight and true.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-layer\">\n<span class=\"vinyl-layer-num\">2</span>\n<strong>1/2\" Plywood</strong>\n<span>Continuous exterior-grade plywood creates the solid wall backing.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-layer\">\n<span class=\"vinyl-layer-num\">3</span>\n<strong>Weather Barrier</strong>\n<span>WRB and flashing help manage incidental water behind the siding.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-layer\">\n<span class=\"vinyl-layer-num\">4</span>\n<strong>Trim System</strong>\n<span>Starter, corners and channels establish the perimeter and receiving points.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-layer\">\n<span class=\"vinyl-layer-num\">5</span>\n<strong>Vinyl Lap Siding</strong>\n<span>Horizontal Forest Ridge courses complete the visible exterior.</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<div class=\"vinyl-best-grid\">\n<section class=\"vinyl-panel\">\n<h3>Well Suited For</h3>\n<ul class=\"vinyl-list\">\n<li>Backyard buildings designed to complement vinyl-sided homes</li>\n<li>Garden buildings and cottages</li>\n<li>Pool houses and backyard retreats</li>\n<li>Traditional storage sheds</li>\n<li>Projects where low routine exterior maintenance is a priority</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"vinyl-panel\">\n<h3>Why Homeowners Choose It</h3>\n<ul class=\"vinyl-list\">\n<li>Traditional horizontal residential appearance</li>\n<li>No routine exterior painting or staining</li>\n<li>Weather- and pest-resistant vinyl material</li>\n<li>Wood-grain surface texture</li>\n<li>Wide range of siding colors</li>\n<li>Full plywood-backed Appalachian wall assembly</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section class=\"vinyl-profile\">\n<h3>Forest Ridge Traditional Lap Profiles</h3>\n<p>Forest Ridge is available in traditional horizontal lap profiles, including Double 4-inch and Double 5-inch configurations. Both create a conventional residential siding appearance; the difference is primarily the width and visual scale of the exposed courses.</p>\n<p>The siding has a nominal .042-inch material thickness and a wood-grain finish. Color availability varies by profile, and some premium colors may carry an additional material cost.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"vinyl-footer\">\n<div class=\"vinyl-footer-copy\">\n<span>What's Behind the Vinyl Matters</span>\n<h3>A Low-Maintenance Exterior Still Deserves a Substantial Wall</h3>\n<p>Vinyl siding provides the finished appearance and weather-resistant exterior surface, but it is not structural wall sheathing. Appalachian Sheds builds the wall first\u2014framing, full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood, weather preparation and flashing\u2014then installs the vinyl siding system over that prepared surface.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vinyl-footer-side\">\n<strong>Georgia-Pacific<br/>Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap<br/>Option 04 of 05</strong>\n</div>\n</section>\n<details class=\"vinyl-tech\">\n<summary>Technical Installation Note <b aria-hidden=\"true\"></b></summary>\n<div class=\"vinyl-tech-body\">\n<p>Georgia-Pacific installation guidance states that vinyl siding should be applied over sheathing that provides a smooth, flat and stable surface and should not be applied directly to wall studs without sheathing. The sheathed wall is prepared with a weather-resistive barrier and integrated flashing before vinyl siding and accessories are installed. Appalachian Sheds' wall-sheathing specification for this siding system is full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-siding-lap-title\" id=\"asi-siding-lap\">\n<div class=\"lap-shell\">\n<header class=\"lap-head\">\n<p class=\"lap-kicker\">Siding &amp; Exterior Finishes \u00b7 Option 05</p>\n<h2 class=\"lap-title\" id=\"asi-siding-lap-title\">LP SmartSide Lap Siding</h2>\n<p class=\"lap-subtitle\">Premium Horizontal Siding \u00b7 Plywood-Backed Wall Assembly</p>\n<p class=\"lap-lede\">LP SmartSide Lap Siding gives an Appalachian building the refined horizontal proportions of traditional residential wood siding while retaining the durability and consistency of an engineered-wood exterior. It is an excellent choice when the goal is to make a shed, cottage, studio, pool house or custom backyard building feel more closely related to the architecture of a home.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"lap-divider\"></div>\n</header><figure aria-label=\"Image position for LP SmartSide Lap Siding\" class=\"asi-siding-photo-slot\" id=\"siding-photo-05\"><div class=\"asi-siding-photo-placeholder\"><span class=\"asi-slot-small\">PHOTOGRAPH POSITION 05 / 05</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-slot-icon\">\u25a7</span><strong>LP SmartSide Lap Siding</strong><span class=\"asi-slot-note\">Approved installed-finish photograph to be supplied</span></div><figcaption><strong>LP SmartSide Lap \u2014 Installed Finish</strong><span>Illustration position reserved; no substitute product photograph used.</span></figcaption></figure>\n<div class=\"lap-intro-grid\">\n<article class=\"lap-copy\">\n<h3 class=\"lap-h3\">A More Residential Engineered-Wood Exterior</h3>\n<p>Horizontal lap siding changes the character of a backyard structure immediately. Rather than emphasizing traditional shed or barn construction, the overlapping horizontal courses create a more residential, cottage-inspired exterior.</p>\n<p>LP SmartSide Lap Siding is particularly effective on buildings with premium windows, fiberglass doors, porches, extended overhangs and other architectural details where the finished structure is intended to complement the home rather than simply function as storage.</p>\n</article>\n<aside aria-label=\"Architectural character\" class=\"lap-character\">\n<span class=\"lap-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Residential. Refined. Warm. Architectural.</h3>\n<p>A strong choice for projects where the backyard building should have the visual presence of a small residential structure rather than a conventional utility shed.</p>\n<div aria-label=\"Suitable building types\" class=\"lap-tags\">\n<span class=\"lap-tag\">Cottages</span>\n<span class=\"lap-tag\">Studios</span>\n<span class=\"lap-tag\">Pool Houses</span>\n<span class=\"lap-tag\">Custom Buildings</span>\n</div>\n</aside>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-benefits\">\n<div class=\"lap-benefit\">\n<strong>Horizontal Profile</strong>\n<span>Overlapping horizontal courses create familiar residential and cottage proportions.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-benefit\">\n<strong>Engineered Wood</strong>\n<span>Provides the character of painted wood siding in an engineered exterior product.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-benefit\">\n<strong>Texture Choices</strong>\n<span>Available in Cedar Texture or Brushed Smooth depending upon the selected product and finish.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-benefit\">\n<strong>Solid Wall Backing</strong>\n<span>Appalachian Sheds installs the system over full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing.</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"lap-install-title\" class=\"lap-install\">\n<div class=\"lap-install-inner\">\n<div class=\"lap-install-copy\">\n<span class=\"lap-mini\">How We Install It</span>\n<h3 id=\"lap-install-title\">We Build the Wall Before We Install the Lap Siding</h3>\n<p>LP permits certain SmartSide Lap Siding products to be installed directly to properly spaced structural wall studs. Appalachian Sheds standardizes on a continuously sheathed wall assembly for this siding system.</p>\n<p>We first sheath the framed wall with full <strong>1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood</strong>, creating a continuous, solid exterior wall surface. The appropriate weather-resistive barrier and flashing are then installed before the starter detail and overlapping horizontal LP SmartSide siding courses are applied.</p>\n<p>This gives the lap siding a continuous plywood-backed wall rather than depending on direct-to-stud attachment or intermittent secondary framing as the primary support surface.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-wall-card\">\n<p class=\"lap-wall-title\">Typical Appalachian Wall Assembly</p>\n<div class=\"lap-spec\">\n<b>Siding Type</b>\n<span>Horizontal LP SmartSide engineered-wood lap siding</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-spec\">\n<b>Wall Backing</b>\n<span>Full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing over the structural wall framing</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-spec\">\n<b>Moisture Layer</b>\n<span>Properly installed weather-resistive barrier and integrated flashing</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-spec\">\n<b>Starter Detail</b>\n<span>Proper starter strip and first-course preparation establish the required siding angle</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-spec\">\n<b>Finish Layer</b>\n<span>Horizontal LP SmartSide lap courses installed with required overlap, fastening and clearances</span>\n</div>\n<p class=\"lap-plywood-note\"><strong>Appalachian Sheds Standard:</strong> LP permits both direct-to-stud installation in qualifying applications and installation over minimum 7/16-category structural sheathing. Appalachian Sheds instead uses full <strong>1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood</strong> as the continuous wall-sheathing specification for this siding system.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"lap-assembly-title\" class=\"lap-assembly\">\n<div class=\"lap-assembly-head\">\n<span>From the Framing Out</span>\n<h3 id=\"lap-assembly-title\">Understanding the LP Lap-Sided Wall</h3>\n<p>The horizontal siding is the visible exterior layer. The complete wall beneath it provides the structural backing and moisture-management foundation for the finished system.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-layers\">\n<div class=\"lap-layer\">\n<span class=\"lap-layer-num\">1</span>\n<strong>Wall Framing</strong>\n<span>The structural framework establishes the wall geometry and support.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-layer\">\n<span class=\"lap-layer-num\">2</span>\n<strong>1/2\" Plywood</strong>\n<span>Continuous exterior-grade plywood creates the solid wall backing.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-layer\">\n<span class=\"lap-layer-num\">3</span>\n<strong>Weather Barrier</strong>\n<span>WRB and flashing manage incidental moisture behind the siding.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-layer\">\n<span class=\"lap-layer-num\">4</span>\n<strong>Starter Detail</strong>\n<span>The starter establishes the correct angle and position of the first siding course.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-layer\">\n<span class=\"lap-layer-num\">5</span>\n<strong>LP Lap Siding</strong>\n<span>Overlapping horizontal engineered-wood courses complete the exterior.</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<div class=\"lap-best-grid\">\n<section class=\"lap-panel\">\n<h3>Well Suited For</h3>\n<ul class=\"lap-list\">\n<li>Country cottages and premium garden buildings</li>\n<li>Backyard offices and studios</li>\n<li>Pool houses and backyard retreats</li>\n<li>Custom buildings designed to complement the home</li>\n<li>Projects where a residential exterior appearance is a priority</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"lap-panel\">\n<h3>Why Homeowners Choose It</h3>\n<ul class=\"lap-list\">\n<li>Residential horizontal siding appearance</li>\n<li>Engineered-wood construction</li>\n<li>Cedar Texture or Brushed Smooth finish options</li>\n<li>Strong compatibility with contrasting trim</li>\n<li>Works naturally with premium doors and windows</li>\n<li>Full plywood-backed Appalachian wall assembly</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section class=\"lap-textures\">\n<h3>Cedar Texture or Brushed Smooth</h3>\n<p><strong>Cedar Texture</strong> provides a more pronounced wood-grain appearance for homeowners who want the character of traditional painted wood siding.</p>\n<p><strong>Brushed Smooth</strong> creates a quieter, cleaner surface that can feel more contemporary while still retaining the proportions of horizontal wood lap siding.</p>\n<p>Availability of texture, width, factory finish and color depends upon the specific LP SmartSide product selected for the project.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"lap-footer\">\n<div class=\"lap-footer-copy\">\n<span>What's Behind the Siding Matters</span>\n<h3>A Residential Exterior Built Over a Complete Wall Assembly</h3>\n<p>LP SmartSide Lap Siding creates the finished appearance, but Appalachian Sheds does not ask the siding itself to substitute for a fully prepared wall. We build the framing, install full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing, complete the required moisture preparation and flashing, and then install the horizontal siding system.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"lap-footer-side\">\n<strong>LP SmartSide<br/>Lap Siding<br/>Option 05 of 05</strong>\n</div>\n</section>\n<details class=\"lap-tech\">\n<summary>Technical Installation Note <b aria-hidden=\"true\"></b></summary>\n<div class=\"lap-tech-body\">\n<p>LP's current instructions permit 38 Series Lap Siding to be attached directly to studs spaced a maximum of 16 inches on center and 76 Series Lap Siding to studs spaced a maximum of 24 inches on center. Both may also be installed over minimum 7/16-category wood structural panel sheathing with framing spaced within the manufacturer's limits. Appalachian Sheds' wall-sheathing specification for this siding system is full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood, followed by the applicable weather-resistive barrier, flashing, starter detail, fastening, overlap and exterior clearance requirements.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-siding-compare-title\" id=\"asi-siding-compare\">\n<div class=\"sc-shell\">\n<!-- ========================================================\n         HEADER\n         ======================================================== -->\n<header class=\"sc-head\">\n<p class=\"sc-kicker\">Siding &amp; Exterior Finishes \u00b7 Final Comparison</p>\n<h2 class=\"sc-title\" id=\"asi-siding-compare-title\">Which Siding Is Right for Your Building?</h2>\n<p class=\"sc-subtitle\">Compare Appearance, Construction &amp; Finish Requirements</p>\n<p class=\"sc-lede\">All five Appalachian siding systems can produce an attractive, durable building. The meaningful differences are architectural character, wall construction, maintenance expectations and how the exterior is finished. Use this guide to narrow the choices before reviewing model-specific pricing.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sc-divider\"></div>\n</header>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         QUICK CHARACTER GUIDE\n         ======================================================== -->\n<div class=\"sc-quick\">\n<div class=\"sc-quick-card\">\n<strong>LP SmartSide Vertical Panel</strong>\n<span>Clean &amp; Traditional</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-quick-card\">\n<strong>Roseburg DuraTemp</strong>\n<span>Real-Wood Character</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-quick-card\">\n<strong>LP Board &amp; Batten</strong>\n<span>Architectural &amp; Dimensional</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-quick-card\">\n<strong>Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap</strong>\n<span>Residential &amp; Low Maintenance</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-quick-card\">\n<strong>LP SmartSide Lap</strong>\n<span>Residential Engineered Wood</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         FULL COMPARISON\n         ======================================================== -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"sc-table-title\" class=\"sc-table-section\">\n<div class=\"sc-table-head\">\n<span>Side-by-Side Comparison</span>\n<h3 id=\"sc-table-title\">Five Siding Systems \u2014 One Clear View</h3>\n<p>On smaller screens, swipe or scroll horizontally to see the complete comparison.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"sc-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Siding</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Exterior Character</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Wall System</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Wall Backing</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Maintenance / Finish</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Best Suited For</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Pricing Position</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding</th>\n<td>Clean vertical lines with straightforward traditional shed and barn character.</td>\n<td>Qualifying structural engineered-wood siding panel.</td>\n<td>The structural siding panel itself can form the continuous exterior wall skin in qualifying applications.</td>\n<td>Field finish requirements depend upon the exact product supplied. Standard ASI building pricing does not include field painting unless specifically stated.</td>\n<td>Classic sheds, garden buildings, workshops, barns and traditional storage structures.</td>\n<td>See selected building model and size pricing.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Roseburg DuraTemp Wood Siding</th>\n<td>Traditional rough-sawn wood character with a substantial shed and barn appearance.</td>\n<td>Real-wood plywood structural siding panel with hardboard face.</td>\n<td>The DuraTemp plywood siding panel can serve as the continuous structural exterior wall skin.</td>\n<td>Requires an appropriate exterior coating system and ongoing finish maintenance. Field finishing is separate unless purchased.</td>\n<td>Classic sheds, barns, workshops, equipment buildings and traditional wood-style structures.</td>\n<td>See selected building model and size pricing.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten Siding</th>\n<td>Deep vertical shadow lines with greater architectural depth and cottage or barn character.</td>\n<td>Applied vertical siding and batten system.</td>\n<td>Full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing used by Appalachian Sheds, followed by the appropriate weather preparation.</td>\n<td>Painted engineered-wood exterior. Field painting and general finish caulking are separate unless included in the Turnkey Exterior Finish Package.</td>\n<td>Country cottages, custom buildings, pool houses, studios, barns and premium backyard structures.</td>\n<td>See selected building model and size pricing.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap Siding</th>\n<td>Traditional horizontal residential siding appearance.</td>\n<td>Nonstructural vinyl exterior cladding.</td>\n<td>Full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing used by Appalachian Sheds, followed by WRB, flashing and vinyl accessories.</td>\n<td>Vinyl color is integral to the siding and does not require routine field painting or staining. Other trim and door components may still require finishing.</td>\n<td>Buildings designed to complement vinyl-sided homes, cottages, pool houses and low-maintenance backyard structures.</td>\n<td>See selected building model and size pricing.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">LP SmartSide Lap Siding</th>\n<td>Refined horizontal engineered-wood appearance with strong residential and cottage character.</td>\n<td>Applied horizontal engineered-wood lap siding.</td>\n<td>Full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood sheathing used by Appalachian Sheds, followed by the appropriate WRB, flashing and starter details.</td>\n<td>Painted engineered-wood exterior. Field painting is separate unless included in the Turnkey Exterior Finish Package.</td>\n<td>Cottages, studios, backyard offices, pool houses and custom buildings designed to complement the home.</td>\n<td>See selected building model and size pricing.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"sc-table-note\">Siding availability, colors, profiles, finishes and pricing may vary by building model, size and current material availability. Final specifications are confirmed in the written project scope.</p>\n</section>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         CHOOSE BY PRIORITY\n         ======================================================== -->\n<section aria-labelledby=\"sc-priority-title\" class=\"sc-priority\">\n<div class=\"sc-section-head\">\n<span>Choose by Priority</span>\n<h3 id=\"sc-priority-title\">What Matters Most to You?</h3>\n<p>Rather than searching for one universal \u201cbest\u201d siding, start with the exterior characteristic that matters most for your building.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-priority-grid\">\n<div class=\"sc-priority-card\">\n<strong>I Want a Simple Traditional Shed Exterior</strong>\n<p>Start with LP SmartSide Vertical Panel or Roseburg DuraTemp. Both create clean vertical proportions without the deeper raised lines of board-and-batten.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-priority-card\">\n<strong>I Want More Architectural Detail</strong>\n<p>LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten adds raised battens, deeper shadows and more visual dimension to cottages, studios and custom structures.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-priority-card\">\n<strong>I Want a Residential Horizontal Look</strong>\n<p>Choose between Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap and LP SmartSide Lap depending upon whether you prefer vinyl or an engineered-wood exterior.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-priority-card\">\n<strong>I Want Real-Wood Plywood Construction</strong>\n<p>Roseburg DuraTemp is a plywood-based siding panel with a rough-sawn exterior face and traditional wood-building character.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-priority-card\">\n<strong>I Want Lower Routine Finish Maintenance</strong>\n<p>Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap avoids the regular field painting or staining associated with painted wood and engineered-wood siding surfaces.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-priority-card\">\n<strong>I Want the Building to Complement My Home</strong>\n<p>Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap or LP SmartSide Lap generally provide the most familiar residential horizontal siding appearance.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         TWO WALL-SYSTEM FAMILIES\n         ======================================================== -->\n<section aria-label=\"Wall construction comparison\" class=\"sc-construction\">\n<div class=\"sc-construction-card\">\n<span>Structural Siding Panels</span>\n<h3>The Siding Can Also Be the Wall Skin</h3>\n<p>LP SmartSide Vertical Panel and Roseburg DuraTemp can perform both the exterior-siding and continuous structural wall-skin functions in qualifying installations. An additional plywood layer is not automatically required simply to provide siding backing.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-construction-card\">\n<span>Applied Siding &amp; Cladding</span>\n<h3>The Finished Siding Goes Over a Prepared Wall</h3>\n<p>For Appalachian Sheds' Board &amp; Batten, Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap and LP SmartSide Lap systems, the wall is first sheathed with full 1/2-inch exterior-grade plywood and then prepared for the applicable weather-management and siding system.</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         FINISH REMINDER\n         ======================================================== -->\n<section class=\"sc-finish\">\n<h3>Field Painting &amp; Staining Are Not Included in Standard Pricing</h3>\n<p>Unless specifically included in the written project scope, field painting, staining and general exterior finish caulking are not included in the standard building price. Appalachian Sheds can provide an optional Turnkey Exterior Finish Package.</p>\n<p><strong>Doors supplied unfinished or requiring field finishing must be sealed or painted within 30 days of construction</strong> unless door finishing is included in the written project scope or the written project scope specifies otherwise.</p>\n</section>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         FINAL PRODUCT LINKS\n         ======================================================== -->\n<div class=\"sc-section-head\">\n<span>Review the Details</span>\n<h3>Return to Any Siding System</h3>\n<p>Each detailed section explains installation, backing, architectural character and recommended applications.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-final-grid\">\n<article class=\"sc-final-card\">\n<strong>LP SmartSide Vertical Panel Siding</strong>\n<p>Clean vertical structural panel siding for straightforward traditional exterior character.</p>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-lpvp\">Review Option 01</a>\n</article>\n<article class=\"sc-final-card\">\n<strong>Roseburg DuraTemp Wood Siding</strong>\n<p>Real-wood plywood structural siding with a traditional rough-sawn exterior appearance.</p>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-dt\">Review Option 02</a>\n</article>\n<article class=\"sc-final-card\">\n<strong>LP SmartSide Board &amp; Batten Siding</strong>\n<p>Dimensional vertical siding over Appalachian's full plywood-backed wall assembly.</p>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-bb\">Review Option 03</a>\n</article>\n<article class=\"sc-final-card\">\n<strong>Georgia-Pacific Forest Ridge Vinyl Lap</strong>\n<p>Residential horizontal vinyl cladding over a fully sheathed and weather-prepared wall.</p>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-vinyl\">Review Option 04</a>\n</article>\n<article class=\"sc-final-card\">\n<strong>LP SmartSide Lap Siding</strong>\n<p>Horizontal engineered-wood siding for refined residential and cottage-inspired buildings.</p>\n<a href=\"#asi-siding-lap\">Review Option 05</a>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- ========================================================\n         FINAL CTA\n         ======================================================== -->\n<section class=\"sc-cta\">\n<div class=\"sc-cta-copy\">\n<span>Ready for the Next Step?</span>\n<h3>Choose Your Building \u2014 Then Compare the Siding Prices</h3>\n<p>Siding prices vary by building model and size. Once you have narrowed your exterior preference, use the pricing page for your selected Appalachian building to compare the exact siding prices available for that size and configuration.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sc-cta-side\">\n<a href=\"/buildings/\">Explore Classic Sheds</a>\n<a class=\"sc-cta-ghost\" href=\"tel:15133792421\">Call Edwin \u00b7 (513) 379-2421</a>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</section>"} />
</Base>

